# Logs
logs/
*.log
# Env
.env
.env.*
# Backup copies of .env made by hand during rotations. These hold LIVE
# credentials in cleartext and the patterns above do not catch them --
# ".env-OLD.txt" matches neither ".env" nor ".env.*". Appeared 2026-09-03.
# This is exactly the shape of REQ-M6HZK4: one `git add -A` from permanent
# history, and git history cannot be scrubbed the way a Doc can.
.env-*
*.env
env.bak
.env.bak
# Credential-bearing one-shot clients -- see Issue Journal REQ-M6HZK4.
# These four scripts and the helper below hardcode the live BUS_SECRET in
# cleartext. They are untracked today; without these lines a single
# `git add -A` would commit the secret into history permanently, and git
# history cannot be swapped the way a Doc can. Ignoring them is a guard,
# NOT the fix -- the values still need scrubbing or the files deleting,
# and that is Mr. Salam's call under REQ-M6HZK4.
establish_inbox.py
onboard_gemini.py
send_dispatch.py
send_chatgpt_drill.py
projects/sfdc24-bus-helper/
# Glasses Intake capture frames (wf=GLASSES-INTAKE). The webcam faces the desk,
# so these JPEGs contain whatever is on screen and on the sticky notes below the
# monitor -- observed 2026-09-02 to include an email address and handwritten
# notes. Staged frames are working data, never repository content. Same lesson
# as REQ-M6HZK4: git history cannot be scrubbed the way a Doc can.
data/
# Security review of the live system. It maps working attack paths into
# sfdc24.com and the bus, so it stays local: Mr. Salam pulled it off the remote
# on 2026-09-03 and it should not go back without him saying so. Same reasoning
# as the entries above -- a push is not undoable the way a local delete is, and
# a repo can change visibility later without anyone re-reading what is in it.
docs/security-review.md
# Same rule, same reason: the multi-agent review repeats the confirmed findings
# (the google.script.run exposure, the visitor-text-into-the-agent-board
# crossing) and is therefore an attack map too. Local only until Mr. Salam says
# otherwise.
docs/multi-agent-review-2026-09-03.md
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# OS / Editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
# Node (if used)
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Quant research venv and cached market data. The venv is 300MB+ of wheels and
# the market cache is vendor data, not repository content.
.venv-quant/

# Legacy/scratch Apps Script exports. This directory is never a deploy input:
# the tracked root .clasp.json points at
# apps-script/governor-page-api/, the repository's reviewed source of truth.
# A local gas/ snapshot may still be retained temporarily for read-only source
# comparison or rollback evidence, so its contents remain ignored and must not
# be deleted by repository cleanup. Keep the empty directory on fresh clones.
gas/*
!gas/.gitkeep

# Salesforce CLI local state.
.sf/

# Machine-local Claude Code permission grants. These are per-surface decisions
# (the VM has clasp authenticated; the laptop and vm-chrome may not), so they
# must not travel with the repo to the other instances.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Self-hosted bus package (blackboard-bus, added on main in 0919735). The
# SQLite file holds live board rows, so it is working data, not repository
# content -- same rule as data/ above.
bus.db*

# Zoom agent OAuth tokens — never commit
zoom-agent/.tokens.json
.tokens.json

# The templates are not secrets - they are how you know what to fill in.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
